[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7112"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=2t-9{t}^{2}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2t-9{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-3{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=-2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =(1)^{2}-3(1)^{3}+C \\\\ -2 & =1-3+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)={t}^{2}-3{t}^{3}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =(2)^{2}-3(2)^{3} \\\\  & =4-24 \\\\  & =-20\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $20\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19486"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. Given that it is at rest when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, find the velocity (in $\\text{m/s}$)  of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-19489/selection/4c5e2d518d88ed9bccf709853cc6c045f70df60111399bdd031140b3528b5acd" :answer/id #uuid "e172556b-a8e8-5b18-b447-8c1e26b8c58f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19489/selection/b67a09c440dc2ba333c2d00445a83d8684407c05c6cd8aecb9729844210bd7fe" :answer/id #uuid "11a56cdf-8f21-555b-80a9-2084e339cf20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.625\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19489/selection/5551b67d765be515499ebb0f08e7c11759e6da3043f7933b353129a6ee8e8159" :answer/id #uuid "43319795-a130-5f4a-91ef-e799d91f4c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19489/selection/29fcd26b6f1c15a7f6dcbfae10ce4fd94d816a35269b96a31c5c6a62181ac628" :answer/id #uuid "909c1bf0-7a2d-5e71-9443-8e878901ad01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.25\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19489/selection/b498caee37af5f377742b7640ded26dfbca31037e4723f4c91433d55b7c54a84" :answer/id #uuid "990d214e-6a5e-55e5-9306-11fef3b5ddc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19489/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd9d928a-ed3b-5f20-aa17-e6eb6628bba2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19489/selection/5551b67d765be515499ebb0f08e7c11759e6da3043f7933b353129a6ee8e8159" :answer-field/choices ["q-19489/selection/4c5e2d518d88ed9bccf709853cc6c045f70df60111399bdd031140b3528b5acd" "q-19489/selection/b67a09c440dc2ba333c2d00445a83d8684407c05c6cd8aecb9729844210bd7fe" "q-19489/selection/5551b67d765be515499ebb0f08e7c11759e6da3043f7933b353129a6ee8e8159" "q-19489/selection/29fcd26b6f1c15a7f6dcbfae10ce4fd94d816a35269b96a31c5c6a62181ac628" "q-19489/selection/b498caee37af5f377742b7640ded26dfbca31037e4723f4c91433d55b7c54a84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19489" :question/id #uuid "66dc2a76-d4e2-534c-99d2-6f4373844378" :question/math-academy-id "q-19489" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t),$ where $a(t)$ is measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and $t$ is measured in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4(-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t))+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=\\frac{4}{5}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)+C \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+C \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 1+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t).$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =-0.8\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $0.8\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-19489/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19489"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351004/field-1/c6f966a0e0451614eb9386b093ea6bbffeeb74f212d2ca4b780924b997f6ebc0" :answer/id #uuid "ade58f70-ab02-5935-ab25-68c6237e338c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3t^5+2t^3-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351004/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "15b03d7c-914a-5bf8-9ca9-acfd2e7f2e87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351004/field-1/c6f966a0e0451614eb9386b093ea6bbffeeb74f212d2ca4b780924b997f6ebc0" :answer-field/choices ["q-351004/field-1/c6f966a0e0451614eb9386b093ea6bbffeeb74f212d2ca4b780924b997f6ebc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351004" :question/id #uuid "dc7a0ebd-53d2-5ffe-8966-1b20839d3b60" :question/math-academy-id "q-351004" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=100\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{5}+2{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=100.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100 & =3({2}^{5})+2({2}^{3})+C \\\\ 100 & =96+16+C \\\\ 100 & =112+C \\\\ C & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{t}^{5}+2{t}^{3}-12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351004/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee2920dc-93e1-5595-a751-62ad5e4f3035"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351004"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
